# Shell scripts and graph files must check out with LF endings on every platform.
#
# Without this, a clone made by Git for Windows (core.autocrlf=true) writes CRLF,
# and the same working tree opened under WSL fails on every script with a bare
# "\r: command not found" — the shebang line itself ends in \r. The graph files
# are listed too so `merge=union` in core/.gitattributes cannot produce a file
# with mixed endings.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.bash  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
